  "user_request_original": "Design a planar multilayer stack with air incidence on an aluminum substrate. Stack sequence from air to substrate: two HfO2/SiO2 (Lemarchand) pairs as top mirror, one chromium layer as cavity defect, two HfO2/SiO2 (Lemarchand) pairs as bottom mirror, terminating at aluminum substrate. Total layer count is 9 (4 dielectric pairs + 1 Cr (Rakic-LD) + Al (Rakic-LD) substrate not counted as film layer). Optimize the thickness of the chromium layer and all dielectric layer thicknesses independently to create a resonant cavity. Wavelength range 400-2000 nm. Target: maximize absorptance in 400-700 nm through cavity resonance, maximize reflectance in 700-2000 nm. Normal incidence, unpolarized light.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 9-layer HfO2/SiO2/Cr/HfO2/SiO2 cavity-on-Al stack (air incidence) over 400–2000 nm at normal unpolarized incidence. Optimize all 9 layer thicknesses to maximize mean absorptance in 400–700 nm and maximize mean reflectance in 700–2000 nm.",
